cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LTRquest, please cite it as below."
title: "LTRquest: iterative detection of nested LTR retrotransposons"
abstract: >-
  LTRquest finds full-length LTR retrotransposons, including elements nested
  inside other elements, by scanning a genome, masking what it found, and
  scanning again. Rounds are reconciled into nesting-depth buckets.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Benson
    given-names: Chris
repository-code: "https://github.com/cwb14/LTRquest"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-21"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - transposable elements
  - LTR retrotransposon
